// A bare `fixed<d,s>` as an attribute type. `attr_spec` takes a
// `param_type_spec`, which has no `fixed_pt_type`: a fixed-point type reaches
// a signature only after a `typedef` gives it a name. omniidl 4.3.4 says
//   Syntax error in interface body
//   Error in look-up of 'balance': 'balance' not found
// (no line number quoted: it moves whenever this comment does).
// The legal neighbour is `typedef fixed<9,2> Amount; attribute Amount balance;`
// — accepted by omniidl, and what corpus/golden/21-deferred-fixed.idl writes.
module n13 { interface Account { attribute fixed<9,2> balance; }; };
